                <head>285. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Democratic Party held its nominating and national convention in the Municipal
                    Theater in Seoul November 26–27. The 970 delegates in a narrow vote selected
                        Cho Pyong-ok as the presidential
                    candidate of the party and Chang Myon
                    as the vice presidential candidate. Chang
                        Myon was subsequently elected Senior Supreme Committeeman over
                        Cho Pyong-ok by a vote of 518 to
                    447. In assessing the conventions in telegram 381 from Seoul, November 27, the
                    Embassy noted that the convention ended on a note of harmony, with
                        Chang and Cho calling on the
                    delegates to put the bitterness of past factionalism aside in the interest of
                    unity and a strong presidential campaign. (Department of State, Central Files,
                    795B.00/11–2759)</p>
            </div>
